    "updated_at": "2026-07-24T18:03:27Z",
    "body": "The reason that we are slotting span elements is so that this works:\n```html\n<select multiple>\n  <span>\n    <option>option</option>\n  </span>\n</select>\n```\nBefore customizable select, there was a conservative slotting algorithm which would only slot options, optgroups, and hr elements, and leave anything else unslotted. With customizable select, I added spans and divs to this.\n\nI guess I'd be fine slotting anything (such as text nodes) as long as it doesn't break any websites, which it probably wouldn't.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/5072951008/reactions",
