    "created_at": "2026-07-24T18:17:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-24T18:17:43Z",
    "body": "> I guess slotting for base appearance right now says text should be slotted, right?\n> \n> > A select popover slot, which is a [slot](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-slot-element) element. It is appended to the [select popover](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#select-popover). It is [expected](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#expected) to take all child nodes of the [select](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-select-element) except for the first child [button](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-button-element), which is taken by the [select button slot](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#select-button-slot).\n\nWe have different slotting algorithms for dropdown selects vs listbox selects: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#select-list-box-slot\n\nAlthough now I see that it does in fact say that it should take all child nodes of the select element, so yeah go ahead and make that WPT and I'll change chromium to unconditionally slot all child nodes for listbox select elements.\n\n> I think slotting decisions shouldn't depend on style, so that should also apply to appearance: auto.\n\nI completely agree. The spec is worded in such a way that the slotting rules only matter for base appearance which doesn't reflect how I've implemented it to not depend on style.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
